 r←GetIndexStamp registryPath;filename;ts;qdmx
⍝ Returns when "tatin_index.txt" was last written, in seconds (⎕DT code 20), or 0 when there
⍝ is no such file - an unmanaged Registry has none.
⍝ `SavePackage` recompiles that index after every successful publish, so this one stat
⍝ answers "has anything been published since I last looked?" without listing the Registry,
⍝ let alone reading a config from every package in it. That matters: this is asked on every
⍝ housekeeping call, and a Registry is expected to grow into the thousands of packages.
 r←0
 filename←registryPath,'/',Reg.Index.GetIndexFilename
 :If F.IsFile filename
     :Trap 19 22
         ts←⊃⊃('type' 3)F.Dir filename
         r←⊃20 ⎕DT⊂ts
     :Else
         qdmx←⎕DMX
         r←0
         LogError'Cannot read the timestamp of "',filename,'": ',qdmx.EM,'; RC=',⍕qdmx.EN
     :EndTrap
 :EndIf
